<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Justus Möser</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1720">1720</a>–<a href="/years/1794">1794</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Justus Möser was a German jurist, historian and essayist who for decades directed the government of the prince-bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osnabruck">Osnabrück</a>. His History of Osnabrück and his Patriotic Fantasies defended local customs and the old estates against centralising reform, and influenced the young Goethe and early German conservatism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/justus-moser.jpg" alt="Justus Möser" width="210" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Justus-moeser_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
